          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            The
            %em supergravity Lie 3-algebra
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝔰𝔲𝔤𝔯𝔞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 10
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{sugra}(10,1)
            or
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M2-brane"} M2-brane
            extension
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝔪
                  %mn 2
                  %mi 𝔟𝔯𝔞𝔫𝔢
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{m}2\mathfrak{brane}
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+L-%E2%88%9E+algebra"} super L-∞ algebra
            that is a shifted
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-Lie+algebra+cohomology"} extension
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 0
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi b
                    %mn 2
                  %mi ℝ
                  %mo →
                  %mi 𝔰𝔲𝔤𝔯𝔞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 10
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi 𝔰𝔦𝔰𝔬
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 10
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  0 \to b^2 \mathbb{R} \to
                  \\mathfrak{sugra}(10,1) \to
                  \\mathfrak{siso}(10,1)
                  \\to
                  0
          %p
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Poincare+Lie+algebra"} super Poincare Lie algebra
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝔰𝔦𝔰𝔬
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 10
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{siso}(10,1)
            in 10+1 dimensions induced by the exceptional degree 4-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebra+cohomology"} super Lie algebra cocycle
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi μ
                    %mn 4
                  %mo =
                  %mover
                    %mi ψ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                  %mo ∧
                  %msup
                    %mi Γ
                    %mrow
                      %mi a
                      %mi b
                  %mi ψ
                  %mo ∧
                  %msub
                    %mi e
                    %mi a
                  %mo ∧
                  %msub
                    %mi e
                    %mi b
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi CE
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝔰𝔦𝔰𝔬
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 10
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mu_4 = \bar \psi \wedge \Gamma^{a b} \psi \wedge e_a \wedge e_b
                  \\;\;
                  \\in CE(\mathfrak{siso}(10,1))
                  \\,.
          %p
            This is the same mechanism by which the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/String+Lie+2-algebra"} String Lie 2-algebra
            is a shifted central extension of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝔰𝔬
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{so}(n)
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#the_chevalleyeilenberg_algebra The Chevalley-Eilenberg algebra
          #TheCEAlgebra.num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chevalley-Eilenberg+algebra"} Chevalley-Eilenberg algebra
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi CE
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝔰𝔲𝔤𝔯𝔞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 10
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CE(\mathfrak{sugra}(10,1))
              is generated on
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  elements
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %msup
                          %mi e
                          %mi a
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{e^a\}
                  and
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %msup
                          %mi ω
                          %mrow
                            %mi a
                            %mi b
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{\omega^{ a b}\}
                  of degree
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %mi even
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (1,even)
              %li
                %p
                  a single element
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi c
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c
                  of degree
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn 3
                        %mo ,
                        %mi even
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (3,even)
              %li
                %p
                  and elements
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %msup
                          %mi ψ
                          %mi α
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{\psi^\alpha\}
                  of degree
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %mi odd
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (1,odd)
            %p with the differential defined by
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi d
                      %mi CE
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %msup
                      %mi ω
                      %mrow
                        %mi a
                        %mi b
                    %mo =
                    %msup
                      %mi ω
                      %mi a
                    %msub
                      %mrow
                      %mi b
                    %mo ∧
                    %msup
                      %mi ω
                      %mrow
                        %mi b
                        %mi c
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    d_{CE} \, \omega^{a b} = \omega^a{}_b \wedge \omega^{b c}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi d
                      %mi CE
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %msup
                      %mi e
                      %mi a
                    %mo =
                    %msup
                      %mi ω
                      %mi a
                    %msub
                      %mrow
                      %mi b
                    %mo ∧
                    %msup
                      %mi e
                      %mi b
                    %mo +
                    %mfrac
                      %mi i
                      %mn 2
                    %mover
                      %mi ψ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                    %msup
                      %mi Γ
                      %mi a
                    %mi ψ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    d_{CE} \, e^{a } = \omega^a{}_b \wedge e^b + \frac{i}{2}\bar \psi \Gamma^a \psi
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi d
                      %mi CE
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi ψ
                    %mo =
                    %mfrac
                      %mn 1
                      %mn 4
                    %msup
                      %mi ω
                      %mrow
                        %mi a
                        %mi b
                    %msub
                      %mi Γ
                      %mrow
                        %mi a
                        %mi b
                    %mi ψ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    d_{CE} \, \psi = \frac{1}{4} \omega^{ a b} \Gamma_{a b} \psi
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi d
                      %mi CE
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi c
                    %mo =
                    %mfrac
                      %mn 1
                      %mn 2
                    %mover
                      %mi ψ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                    %msup
                      %mi Γ
                      %mrow
                        %mi a
                        %mi b
                    %mo ∧
                    %mi ψ
                    %mo ∧
                    %msub
                      %mi e
                      %mi a
                    %mo ∧
                    %msub
                      %mi e
                      %mi b
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    d_{CE} \, c = \frac{1}{2}\bar \psi \Gamma^{a b} \wedge \psi \wedge e_a \wedge e_b
                    \\,.
          %blockquote
            %p (fill in details)
          %h3#hidden_super_lie_1algebra Hidden super Lie 1-algebra
          %p
            At the end of (
            %a{:href => "#DAuriaFr82"}> D’Auria-Fre 82
            ) the authors ask for a super Lie 1-algebra
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝔤
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            in its
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chevalley-Eilenberg+algebra"} Chevalley-Eilenberg algebra
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi 𝔤
                  %mo ⟶
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mrow
                      %mn 10
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mn 32
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p\colon \mathfrak{g}\longrightarrow \mathbb{R}^{10,1\vert \mathbf{32}}
            such that the pullback of the 4-cocycle
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi μ
                    %mn 4
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu_4
            along
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            is trivialized by
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi p
                    %mo *
                  %msub
                    %mi μ
                    %mn 4
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi d
                    %mi CE
                  %mi A
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  p^\ast \mu_4 = d_{CE}A
                  \\,.
          %p
            In the
            %span.newWikiWord
              homotopy theory of L-infinity algebras
              %a{:href => "/nlab/new/model+structure+on+L-infinity+algebras"} ?
            this means that
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi 𝔤
                        %mtd
                          %mo ⟶
                        %mtd
                          %mo *
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mrow
                            %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                              %mi p
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mo ⇙
                            %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                              %mi A
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mi ℝ
                            %mrow
                              %mn 10
                              %mo ,
                              %mn 1
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                              %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                %mn 32
                        %mtd
                          %munder
                            %mo ⟶
                            %mrow
                              %msub
                                %mi μ
                                %mn 4
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi B
                            %mn 3
                          %mi ℝ
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  \\mathfrak{g} &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; \ast
                  \\\
                  {}^{\mathllap{p}}
                  \\downarrow
                  \&amp;\swArrow_{\mathrlap{A}}&amp;
                  \\downarrow
                  \\\
                  \\mathbb{R}^{10,1\vert \mathbf{32}}
                  \&amp;\underset{\mu_4}{\longrightarrow}&amp;
                  \\mathbf{B}^3 \mathbb{R}
                  }
                  \\,.
          %p
            Compare this to the characterization of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝔰𝔲𝔤𝔯𝔞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 10
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{sugra}(10,1)
            as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+fiber"} homotopy fiber
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi μ
                      %mn 4
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu_4
            %em universal
            solution to this situation
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi 𝔰𝔲𝔤𝔯𝔞
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mn 10
                          %mo ,
                          %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mo ⟶
                        %mtd
                          %mo *
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mo ⇙
                            %mrow
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mi ℝ
                            %mrow
                              %mn 10
                              %mo ,
                              %mn 1
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                              %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                %mn 32
                        %mtd
                          %munder
                            %mo ⟶
                            %mrow
                              %msub
                                %mi μ
                                %mn 4
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi B
                            %mn 3
                          %mi ℝ
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  \\mathfrak{sugra}(10,1) &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; \ast
                  \\\
                  \\downarrow
                  \&amp;\swArrow_{}&amp;
                  \\downarrow
                  \\\
                  \\mathbb{R}^{10,1\vert \mathbf{32}}
                  \&amp;\underset{\mu_4}{\longrightarrow}&amp;
                  \\mathbf{B}^3 \mathbb{R}
                  }
                  \\,.
          %p
            In any case, in (
            %a{:href => "#DAuriaFr82"}> D’Auria-Fre 82
            ) possible choices for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi 𝔤
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mrow
                      %mn 10
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mn 32
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p \colon \mathfrak{g} \to \mathbb{R}^{10,1\vert\mathbf{32}}
            are found.
          %p
            Curiously, the bosonic
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/body"} body
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝔤
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
            is such that when adapted to a compactification to 4d, then it is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exceptional+tangent+bundle"} exceptional tangent bundle
            on which the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/U-duality"} U-duality
            group
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/E7"} E7
            has a canonical action.
          %p
            In (
            %a{:href => "#BAIPV04"}> BAIPV 04
            ) these solutions are shown to extend to a 1-parameter family of solutions. Further comments are in (
            %a{:href => "#AndrianopoliDAuriaRavera16"}> Andrianopoli-D’Auria-Ravera 16
            ).
