            %h3#the_brane_molecule The Brane molecule
            %p
              Furthermore, there exists a more general classification of possible supermembranes in spacetime with
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              spatial dimensions and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
              time dimensions, appearing in (
              %a{:href => "#BlencoweDuff88"}> Blencowe-Duff 88
              ). In this sense, the brane scan is but the
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                    %mo =
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T=1
              branch of the brane molecule. The objects appearing here are expected to be related to other generalizations of string theory. See
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D%3D12+supergravity"} D=12 supergravity
              and
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bosonic+M-theory"} bosonic M-theory
            %p
              %img{:alt => "The brane molecule without assuming super Poincare invariance.", :src => "/nlab/files/branemoleculepc.png"}/
            %p Compare:
            %ul
              %li#BlencoweDuff88
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Miles+Blencowe"}> Miles Blencowe
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mike+Duff"} Mike Duff
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em Supermembranes and the Signature of Space-time
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a{:href => "inspirehep.net/record/262142"} spire:262142
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/0550-3213(88)90155-1"} 10.1016/0550-3213(88)90155-1
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a{:href => "http://inspirehep.net/record/262142/files/cer-000099708.pdf"} pdf
              %li
                %p
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/brane+bouquet"} brane bouquet
          %h3#Polyvector Relation to the 11-dimensional polyvector super Poincaré-algebra
          %h4#via_derivations Via derivations
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝔡𝔢𝔯
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝔰𝔲𝔤𝔯𝔞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 10
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{der}(\mathfrak{sugra}(10,1))
              be the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/automorphism+%E2%88%9E-Lie+algebra"} automorphism ∞-Lie algebra
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝔰𝔲𝔤𝔯𝔞
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 10
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{sugra}(10,1)
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dg-Lie+algebra"} dg-Lie algebra
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝔡𝔢𝔯
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝔰𝔲𝔤𝔯𝔞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 10
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{der}(\mathfrak{sugra}(10,1))_0
              for the ordinary
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebra"} Lie algebra
              in degree 0.
            %p
              This is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphic"} isomorphic
              to the polyvector-extension of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Poincar%C3%A9+Lie+algebra"} super Poincaré Lie algebra
              (see there) in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi d
                    %mo =
                    %mn 10
                    %mo +
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d = 10+1
              – the “
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-theory+super+Lie+algebra"}> M-theory super Lie algebra
              ” – with “2-brane central charge”: the Lie algebra spanned by generators
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi P
                      %mi a
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi Q
                      %mi α
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi J
                      %mrow
                        %mi a
                        %mi b
                    %mo ,
                    %msup
                      %mi Z
                      %mrow
                        %mi a
                        %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{P_a, Q_\alpha, J_{a b}, Z^{a b}\}
              and graded Lie brackets those of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Poincar%C3%A9+Lie+algebra"} super Poincaré Lie algebra
              as well as
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msub
                      %mi Q
                      %mi α
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi Q
                      %mi β
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo =
                    %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %msup
                      %mi Γ
                      %mi a
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
                        %mi α
                        %mi β
                    %msub
                      %mi P
                      %mi a
                    %mo +
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %msub
                      %mi Γ
                      %mrow
                        %mi a
                        %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msup
                      %mi Z
                      %mrow
                        %mi a
                        %mi b
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    [Q_\alpha, Q_\beta] = i (C \Gamma^a)_{\alpha \beta} P_a + (C \Gamma_{a b})Z^{a b}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msub
                      %mi Q
                      %mi α
                    %mo ,
                    %msup
                      %mi Z
                      %mrow
                        %mi a
                        %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo =
                    %mn 2
                    %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %msup
                      %mi Γ
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi a
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
                        %mi α
                        %mi β
                    %msup
                      %mi Q
                      %mrow
                        %mi b
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mi β
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    [Q_\alpha, Z^{a b}] = 2 i (C \Gamma^{[a})_{\alpha \beta}Q^{b]\beta}
            %p etc.
          %p
            This observation appears implicitly in (
            %a{:href => "#Castellani05"}> Castellani 05, section 3.1
            ), see (
            %a{:href => "#FSS13"}> FSS 13
            ).
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              With the presentation of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chevalley-Eilenberg+algebra"} Chevalley-Eilenberg algebra
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi CE
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝔰𝔲𝔤𝔯𝔞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 10
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CE(\mathfrak{sugra}(10,1))
              as in prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TheCEAlgebra"}
              above, the generators are identified with
              = succeed "s" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derivation"} derivation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi CE
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝔰𝔲𝔤𝔯𝔞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 10
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CE(\mathfrak{sugra}(10,1))
              as
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi P
                      %mi a
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msub
                      %mi d
                      %mi CE
                    %mo ,
                    %mfrac
                      %mo ∂
                      %mrow
                        %mo ∂
                        %msup
                          %mi e
                          %mi a
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    P_a = [d_{CE}, \frac{\partial}{\partial e^a} ]
            %p and
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Q
                      %mi α
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msub
                      %mi d
                      %mi CE
                    %mo ,
                    %mfrac
                      %mo ∂
                      %mrow
                        %mo ∂
                        %msup
                          %mi ψ
                          %mi α
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Q_\alpha = [d_{CE}, \frac{\partial}{\partial \psi^\alpha} ]
            %p and
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi J
                      %mrow
                        %mi a
                        %mi b
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msub
                      %mi d
                      %mi CE
                    %mo ,
                    %mfrac
                      %mo ∂
                      %mrow
                        %mo ∂
                        %msup
                          %mi ω
                          %mrow
                            %mi a
                            %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    J_{a b} = [d_{CE}, \frac{\partial}{\partial \omega^{a b}} ]
            %p and
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Z
                      %mrow
                        %mi a
                        %mi b
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msub
                      %mi d
                      %mi CE
                    %mo ,
                    %msup
                      %mi e
                      %mi a
                    %mo ∧
                    %msup
                      %mi e
                      %mi b
                    %mo ∧
                    %mfrac
                      %mo ∂
                      %mrow
                        %mo ∂
                        %mi c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Z^{a b} = [d_{CE}, e^a \wedge e^b \wedge \frac{\partial}{\partial c}]
            %p etc. With this it is straightforward to compute the commutators. Notably the last term in
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msub
                      %mi Q
                      %mi α
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi Q
                      %mi β
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo =
                    %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %msup
                      %mi Γ
                      %mi a
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
                        %mi α
                        %mi β
                    %msub
                      %mi P
                      %mi a
                    %mo +
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %msub
                      %mi Γ
                      %mrow
                        %mi a
                        %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msup
                      %mi Z
                      %mrow
                        %mi a
                        %mi b
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    [Q_\alpha, Q_\beta] = i (C \Gamma^a)_{\alpha \beta} P_a + (C \Gamma_{a b})Z^{a b}
            %p
              arises from the contraction of the 4-cocycle
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi ψ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                    %msup
                      %mi Γ
                      %mrow
                        %mi a
                        %mi b
                    %mo ∧
                    %mi ψ
                    %mo ∧
                    %msub
                      %mi e
                      %mi a
                    %mo ∧
                    %msub
                      %mi e
                      %mi b
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bar \psi \Gamma^{a b} \wedge \psi \wedge e_a \wedge e_b
              with
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mfrac
                        %mo ∂
                        %mrow
                          %mo ∂
                          %msup
                            %mi ψ
                            %mi α
                      %mo ∧
                      %mfrac
                        %mo ∂
                        %mrow
                          %mo ∂
                          %msup
                            %mi ψ
                            %mi β
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \frac{\partial}{\partial \psi^\alpha}\wedge \frac{\partial}{\partial \psi^\beta}
          %h4#via_the_heisenberg_lie_3algebras Via the Heisenberg Lie 3-algebras
          %p (…)
          %h2#applications Applications
          %p
            The field configurations of 11-dimensional
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergravity"} supergravity
            may be identified with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-Lie+algebra-valued+forms"} ∞-Lie algebra-valued forms
            with values in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝔰𝔲𝔤𝔯𝔞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 10
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{sugra}(10,1)
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D%27Auria-Fre+formulation+of+supergravity"} D'Auria-Fre formulation of supergravity
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %p
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergravity+Lie+6-algebra"} supergravity Lie 6-algebra
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo →
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \to
            %strong supergravity Lie 3-algebra
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo →
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Poincar%C3%A9+Lie+algebra"} super Poincaré Lie algebra
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D%3D4+supergravity+Lie+2-algebra"} D=4 supergravity Lie 2-algebra
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extended+supersymmetry"} extended supersymmetry
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+II+supergravity+Lie+2-algebra"} type II supergravity Lie 2-algebra
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+II+supersymmetry+algebra"} type II supersymmetry algebra
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-theory+supersymmetry+algebra"} M-theory supersymmetry algebra
          %h2#references References
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chevalley-Eilenberg+algebra"} Chevalley-Eilenberg algebra
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝔰𝔲𝔤𝔯𝔞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 10
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{sugra}(10,1)
            first appears in (3.15) of
          %ul
            %li#DAuriaFr82
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riccardo+D%27Auria"}> Riccardo D'Auria
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pietro+Fr%C3%A9"} Pietro Fré
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/GeometricSupergravity.pdf", :title => "Geometric Supergravity in D=11 and its hidden supergroup"} Geometric Supergravity in D=11 and its hidden supergroup
          %p and later in the textbook
          %ul
            %li#CastellaniDAuriaFre
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Leonardo+Castellani"}> Leonardo Castellani
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riccardo+D%27Auria"} Riccardo D'Auria
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pietro+Fr%C3%A9"} Pietro Fré
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Supergravity+and+Superstrings+-+A+Geometric+Perspective"} Supergravity and Superstrings - A Geometric Perspective
          %p
            The manifest interpretation of this as a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+3-algebra"} Lie 3-algebra
            and the supergravity field content as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-Lie+algebra+valued+forms"} ∞-Lie algebra valued forms
            with values in this is mentioned in
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hisham+Sati"}> Hisham Sati
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"} Urs Schreiber
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jim+Stasheff"} Jim Stasheff
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/L-%E2%88%9E+algebra+connections"} L-∞ algebra connections
            %li#FSS13
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Domenico+Fiorenza"}> Domenico Fiorenza
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hisham+Sati"} Hisham Sati
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"} Urs Schreiber
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/The+brane+bouquet"} Super Lie n-algebra extensions, higher WZW models and super p-branes with tensor multiplet fields
          %p
            A systematic study of the super-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebra+cohomology"} Lie algebra cohomology
            involved is in
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Baez"}> John Baez
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Huerta"} John Huerta
                %em Division algebras and supersymmetry I
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0909.0551"}> arXiv:0909.0551
                )
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Baez"}> John Baez
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Huerta"} John Huerta
                %em Division algebras and supersymmetry II
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1003.3436"}> arXiv:1003.34360
                )
          %p
            See also
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/division+algebra+and+supersymmetry"} division algebra and supersymmetry
          %p Further discussion of its “hidden” super Lie algebra includes
          %ul
            %li#BAIPV04
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Igor+Bandos"}> Igor Bandos
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jos%C3%A9+de+Azc%C3%A1rraga"} José de Azcárraga
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jos%C3%A9+M.+Izquierdo"} José M. Izquierdo
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    On the underlying gauge group structure of
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi D
                          %mo =
                          %mn 11
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D=11
                    supergravity
                %strong 596
                (2004) 145-155 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0406020"}> arXiv;hep-th/0406020
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Igor+Bandos"}> Igor Bandos
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jose+de+Azcarraga"} Jose de Azcarraga
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    On the formulation of
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi D
                          %mo =
                          %mn 11
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D=11
                    supergravity and the composite nature of its three-from field
                %strong 317
                (2005) 238-279 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0409100"}> arXiv:hep-th/0409100
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li#AndrianopoliDAuriaRavera16
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Laura+Andrianopoli"}> Laura Andrianopoli
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riccardo+D%27Auria"} Riccardo D'Auria
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lucrezia+Ravera"} Lucrezia Ravera
                %em Hidden Gauge Structure of Supersymmetric Free Differential Algebras
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1606.07328"}> arXiv:1606.07328
                \&amp;rbrack;
          %p Further review:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lucrezia+Ravera"}> Lucrezia Ravera
              ,
              %em
                On the hidden symmetries of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi D
                      %mo =
                      %mn 11
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D=11
                supergravity
              \&amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2112.00445"}> arXiv:2112.00445
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            The computation of the automorphism Lie algebra of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝔰𝔲𝔤𝔯𝔞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 10
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{sugra}(10,1)
            is in
          %ul
            %li#Castellani05
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Leonardo+Castellani"}> Leonardo Castellani
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Lie derivatives along antisymmetric tensors and the M-theory superalgebra
              %strong 3
              (2011) 1-7 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0508213"}> arXiv:hep-th/0508213
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            A similar argument with more explicit use of the Lie 3-algebra as underlying the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Green-Schwarz+action+functional"} Green-Schwarz-like action functional
            for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M5-brane"} M5-brane
            is in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dmitri+Sorokin"}> Dmitri Sorokin
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paul+Townsend"} Paul Townsend
              = succeed "," do
                %em M-theory superalgebra from the M-5-brane
              %strong 412
              (1997) 265-273 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9708003"}> arXiv:hep-th/9708003
              \&amp;rbrack;
        .revisedby
